From 13cb89a9032f17562b74bd82eefee57baccf4b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:19:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] nvk: build for Windows with the RM backend only

NVK cross-compiles for Windows x86_64 (MinGW-w64) with -Dplatforms=windows
-Dnvk-rm=enabled and produces vulkan_nouveau.dll, which exports only the
loader-ICD interface. Linux builds are unchanged.

 - with_nouveau_drm (false on Windows) leaves out nouveau's DRM winsys and
   nvkmd/nouveau; NVK without nouveau requires -Dnvk-rm=enabled. The
   chipset limits the RM backend needs move from nouveau_device.c to
   nouveau_device_limits.[ch], which have no DRM dependency and are built
   everywhere.
 - The RM backend's DRM side (nvidia-drm node discovery, dma-buf export and
   import, GEM handles) moves from nvkmd_rm_pdev.c, nvkmd_rm_mem.c and
   nvkmd_rm_dev.c to nvkmd_rm_drm.c, built only with NVK_RM_WITH_DRM
   (Linux). Without it nvkmd_rm.h supplies stubs: no dma-bufs and no
   DRM format modifiers (has_alloc_tiled is false), so no
   VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier, no external memory fds.
 - VK_EXT_physical_device_drm and the DRM major/minor properties, and DRM
   syncobj payload copies, are Linux-only.
 - drm-uapi/drm_fourcc.h (NIL's modifier definitions) pulls in drm.h, which
   wants <sys/ioccom.h> off Linux: nouveau's targets get an empty one from
   src/nouveau/compat/win32 on Windows.
 - <windows.h> defines TRUE and FALSE, which nvk_format.c's VA_FMT() would
   expand before pasting them into class field names: undefined there.
 - <sys/mman.h> was included but unused in nvk_descriptor_table.c, and only
   needed for close() (<unistd.h>) in nvk_device_memory.c.
 - vulkan_nouveau.dll: no "lib" prefix, matching the ICD manifest, and
   vulkan_api.def as the export list (as lavapipe and dozen).
